rac{(y+5)^{2}}{3} & =\\frac{49}{7} \\\\ 4+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{6} & =7 \\\\ \\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{3} & =3 \\\\ (y+5)^{2} & =9 \\\\ y+5 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ y & =-5\\pm 3 \\\\ y & =-8,-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $y$-axis are $(0,-8,0)$ and $(0,-2,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-176833/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2e0b4012-403b-5739-8f33-3c79111129fd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-176833"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94486/selection/c5d2f5c9555fba2320659c0637b53770dc75c78695d24aeb53f9a43126fbe51d" :answer/id #uuid "b58d23c4-5e30-5306-8529-4cdd4556b110" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{9}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94486/selection/e1bd6c724a655faf8b2dda41a34f931d0729c9978fab644c09645713b93fc35a" :answer/id #uuid "3a252632-dc8a-5ba2-95ab-6e022446003c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-\\frac{y}{3}\\pm 1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94486/selection/a31f552fce64f9c584df6ffff775cc29d6ede418981d1aecead604648b78387e" :answer/id #uuid "e66722e2-4447-58b6-b28a-6513edf71490" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-\\frac{y}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94486/selection/ae56d4332056d4e5008d8b12f205d90853bb3587a6d473225d13cbf14d1e517f" :answer/id #uuid "9354c474-e593-5dc5-88a5-b62bae7ac79c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94486/selection/58dab47c82961a44bcc8403630e39cd619e70efca00316dd46791e16c5a2e979" :answer/id #uuid "2bcab5e5-4bc7-5832-80ce-3868ed6012c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\pm \\frac{y}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94486/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c5fa9f76-fa14-5642-b2f2-2a3609a1b5c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94486/selection/58dab47c82961a44bcc8403630e39cd619e70efca00316dd46791e16c5a2e979" :answer-field/choices ["q-94486/selection/c5d2f5c9555fba2320659c0637b53770dc75c78695d24aeb53f9a43126fbe51d" "q-94486/selection/e1bd6c724a655faf8b2dda41a34f931d0729c9978fab644c09645713b93fc35a" "q-94486/selection/a31f552fce64f9c584df6ffff775cc29d6ede418981d1aecead604648b78387e" "q-94486/selection/ae56d4332056d4e5008d8b12f205d90853bb3587a6d473225d13cbf14d1e517f" "q-94486/selection/58dab47c82961a44bcc8403630e39cd619e70efca00316dd46791e16c5a2e979"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94486" :question/id #uuid "f1ca6c81-c90d-53e2-91fd-a40e8a96a96b" :question/math-academy-id "q-94486" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cone $\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}={z}^{2}\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{y}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $yz$-plane with equations $z=\\pm \\frac{y}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94486/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb7148a2-58cc-5023-845c-435b47e31c83"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94486"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-95462/selection/4b548ad4c9c9eedb3a544efc897a4ae00c1a487b80085639b1455ac7d361c95f" :answer/id #uuid "2bed8085-5d30-5066-8048-b64efc5400ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-\\frac{1}{4}x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95462/selection/fac643dcefa17e0ac9e0c5a5cb2ccb62d8799b5ea1a66da1281229d6efc84507" :answer/id #uuid "3e0facec-10c0-56c1-99df-92f1b8a262b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\pm 4(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95462/selection/a122d477dea849897fe124726e57cd556b93a2c919e036a5b3d1be063ae6c1bc" :answer/id #uuid "b791444e-da5c-5336-a644-4dc58497467a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=\\pm \\frac{1}{4}(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95462/selection/d7c8d381a7196c3e647da5f8f9a3e773355e59d982d06e7aaf55587dc9d7ce95" :answer/id #uuid "c4c0303f-4f81-575e-ae8d-8f50352a6661" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=-4x+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95462/selection/200d976f35294bc30d6a43f2812f3e6d46c0d151e4e7ad5615493620c86dc5cb" :answer/id #uuid "0411e661-3f7a-5479-b0ad-14a233702b24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "z=4x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-95462/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b1fdddbe-c0c6-5329-b5e8-57c784708b60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-95462/selection/fac643dcefa17e0ac9e0c5a5cb2ccb62d8799b5ea1a66da1281229d6efc84507" :answer-field/choices ["q-95462/selection/4b548ad4c9c9eedb3a544efc897a4ae00c1a487b80085639b1455ac7d361c95f" "q-95462/selection/fac643dcefa17e0ac9e0c5a5cb2ccb62d8799b5ea1a66da1281229d6efc84507" "q-95462/selection/a122d477dea849897fe124726e57cd556b93a2c919e036a5b3d1be063ae6c1bc" "q-95462/selection/d7c8d381a7196c3e647da5f8f9a3e773355e59d982d06e7aaf55587dc9d7ce95" "q-95462/selection/200d976f35294bc30d6a43f2812f3e6d46c0d151e4e7ad5615493620c86dc5cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-95462" :question/id #uuid "3b5c5f76-89be-5d6d-8365-ed748f50ee8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95462" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cone $(x-1)^{2}+7{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{16}{z}^{2}\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+7(0)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{16}{z}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{16}{z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}z & =\\pm (x-1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 4(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z=\\pm 4(x-1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-95462/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb7148a2-58cc-5023-845c-435b47e31c83"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-95462"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-35266/selection/a9c9f9d02b9fd65ec6dd2a9001544798e42ff65c13f2d26ff41ad135b1d901bd" :answer/id #uuid "c6d7f5aa-1429-545d-bab7-1ae2d320c367" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,0,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35266/selection/1ee5ea6feb63629548ed4c79ec2a967b1f27afe29f56c6f3023de971239bad06" :answer/id #uuid "348cabea-f511-560f-8379-34e3aa4c7756" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,\\sqrt{2},\\sqrt{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35266/selection/d3828747ed0964abdfc160c90292fb5f37309822704d5f7c6692030e37326aa4" :answer/id #uuid "3ab5c47f-90d5-5059-ae58-15ac8d2bb229" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(\\sqrt{2}+1,1,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35266/selection/56ca678dcfc5e451909d3b213063f8df3a4e7c70a54799d867f176c7ed37c387" :answer/id #uuid "634288e4-9e2f-50e8-b81a-1ec3d26996e0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,1,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35266/selection/d82015c309897c1b0c40fbad46470c7d5228246f81e0942d781185c7213e6903" :answer/id #uuid "ef3fe25a-f1e9-5539-82b2-6340149ddab1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,0,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-35266/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "77f7d43d-2160-5d79-b283-3fe99241f725" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-35266/selection/a9c9f9d02b9fd65ec6dd2a9001544798e42ff65c13f2d26ff41ad135b1d901bd" :answer-field/choices ["q-35266/selection/a9c9f9d02b9fd65ec6dd2a9001544798e42ff65c13f2d26ff41ad135b1d901bd" "q-35266/selection/1ee5ea6feb63629548ed4c79ec2a967b1f27afe29f56c6f3023de971239bad06" "q-35266/selection/d3828747ed0964abdfc160c90292fb5f37309822704d5f7c6692030e37326aa4" "q-35266/selection/56ca678dcfc5e451909d3b213063f8df3a4e7c70a54799d867f176c7ed37c387" "q-35266/selection/d82015c309897c1b0c40fbad46470c7d5228246f81e0942d781185c7213e6903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-35266" :question/id #uuid "8cf1e2a7-da38-57ea-b1de-04392dc7110c" :question/math-academy-id "q-35266" :question/problem "Given that the trace of the elliptic cone $\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}={z}^{2}$ and the $xz$-plane are two lines, what is the intersection point of these lines?" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0)^{2}}{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ \\pm \\frac{x-1}{2} & =z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z=\\frac{x-1}{2}$ and $z=\\frac{1-x}{2}.$ \n\nTo find the point of intersection of both lines, we equate the right-hand sides. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{2} & =\\frac{1-x}{2} \\\\ x-1 & =1-x \\\\ 2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=1$ in the equation of the first line and solving for $z,$ we obtain $z=\\frac{1-1}{2}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(1,0,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-35266/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb7148a2-58cc-5023-845c-435b47e31c83"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-35266"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-35596"] :question/problem "What is the trace in the $yz$-plane of the elliptic cone $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=(z-4)^{2}\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $yz$-plane, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =(z-4)^{2} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =(z-4)^{2} \\\\ \\pm \\frac{y}{2} & =z-4 \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{y}{2}+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $yz$-plane with equations $z=\\pm \\frac{y}{2}+4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-94496/selection/e3678a7403f3490088348f6695eecfe19c3c7d32d92f8a6384f93e5e692b18e4" :answer/id #uuid "61a18a56-0239-5d46-8788-0a8784686fb8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\frac{2x}{3}+18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94496/selection/1bfd82341cda2f42829bc6293ac0b6a9967de062bd7a6d194cf9d40645d318ed" :answer/id #uuid "3bbb7abe-2515-5225-9c40-7157c703dc7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm \\frac{x}{3}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94496/selection/b2877db6e461cda3ccc2730d8229b34c454f67b4755954ee5c32a5463a875f25" :answer/id #uuid "d26f7178-7b4e-5b40-8a2c-cc56c1d45308" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(9,2,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94496/selection/6877672b9454ac6fbb9ac020675ce557a01e375ea432c7306c5700145f4d2a22" :answer/id #uuid "1439a00c-5fd7-5ff4-9c05-375ae54375db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\pm 3x-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94496/selection/f50e5440fb7b9de72d88a173895ce9db174c4158af1746b78db5a7af9624c6ae" :answer/id #uuid "d969eee5-49d4-52a4-be96-91ac7e08a1b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,0,0)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94496/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "02c90aa7-a97d-5728-ab71-1585eaef3c3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94496/selection/f50e5440fb7b9de72d88a173895ce9db174c4158af1746b78db5a7af9624c6ae" :answer-field/choices ["q-94496/selection/e3678a7403f3490088348f6695eecfe19c3c7d32d92f8a6384f93e5e692b18e4" "q-94496/selection/1bfd82341cda2f42829bc6293ac0b6a9967de062bd7a6d194cf9d40645d318ed" "q-94496/selection/b2877db6e461cda3ccc2730d8229b34c454f67b4755954ee5c32a5463a875f25" "q-94496/selection/6877672b9454ac6fbb9ac020675ce557a01e375ea432c7306c5700145f4d2a22" "q-94496/selection/f50e5440fb7b9de72d88a173895ce9db174c4158af1746b78db5a7af9624c6ae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94496" :question/id #uuid "6734b6c1-1fe4-5e74-9521-784543a97764" :question/math-academy-id "q-94496" :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xy$-plane of the elliptic cone $9(x-2)^{2}+2{y}^{2}=18{z}^{2}\\,?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xy$-plane, we substitute $z=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(x-2)^{2}+2{y}^{2}=18(0)^{2} \\\\ 9(x-2)^{2}+2{y}^{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives in the $xy$-plane the point $(2,0,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-94496/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb7148a2-58cc-5023-845c-435b47e31c83"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94496"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8216"] :question/problem "Given the elliptic cone $\\dfrac{(x-2)^2}{4} + \\dfrac{(y-2)^2}{2} = \\dfrac{(z+1)^2}{3},$ find its intercepts with the $z$-axis." :question/worked-solution "To find the $z$-intercepts of the elliptic cone, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation and solve for $z\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(0-2)^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{4}{4}+\\frac{4}{2} & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ 1+2 & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3} \\\\ 9 & =(z+1)^{2} \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ z & =-1\\pm 3 \\\\ z & =-4,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-4)$ and $(0,0,2).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-8217"] :question/problem "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cone $3x^2 +  4y ^2=12(z+3)^2\\: ?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+4\\cdot {0}^{2} & =12(z+3)^{2} \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & =12(z+3)^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(z+3)^{2} \\\\ \\pm x & =2(z+3) \\\\ \\pm \\frac{x}{2} & =z+3 \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{x}{2}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z = \\pm\\dfrac{x}{2}-3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
